  "scenes": [
    {
      "narration": "It sounds insane, but many countries actively want their own currency to be worth less. On purpose.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "hook",
          "art": "flagStack",
          "country": "cn",
          "trend": "down",
          "props": [
            "chartDown",
            "globe"
          ],
          "lines": [
            "They want it",
            "worth less?"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s1"
    },
    {
      "narration": "The reason is exports. A weaker currency makes everything a country sells cheaper for foreign buyers.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "truth",
          "art": "globe",
          "kicker": "the export trick",
          "line": "Cheaper exports",
          "sub": "a weak currency sells more abroad"
        }
      ],
      "id": "s2"
    },
    {
      "narration": "Exports are goods produced at home and sold to buyers in other countries.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "evidence",
          "sourceId": "wiki-export",
          "kicker": "Wikipedia · export"
        }
      ],
      "id": "s3"
    },
    {
      "narration": "So a weaker currency can mean more factory orders, more jobs, and a bigger trade surplus.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "stat",
          "art": "flagStack",
          "country": "jp",
          "trend": "down",
          "big": "+exports",
          "label": "the weak-currency payoff",
          "props": [
            "chartUp",
            "bill"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s4"
    },
    {
      "narration": "Deliberately lowering a currency's value even has a name, devaluation.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "evidence",
          "sourceId": "wiki-devaluation",
          "kicker": "Wikipedia · devaluation"
        }
      ],
      "id": "s5"
    },
    {
      "narration": "When several countries try it at once, you get a race to the bottom, a currency war.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "flash",
          "bg": "red",
          "line": "Currency war",
          "props": [
            "fire",
            "globe"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s6"
    },
    {
      "narration": "That's when countries compete to weaken their money for a trade advantage.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "evidence",
          "sourceId": "wiki-currencywar",
          "kicker": "Wikipedia · currency war"
        }
      ],
      "id": "s7"
    },
    {
      "narration": "A strong currency flatters the headlines, but a weaker one can quietly sell far more cars and steel abroad.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "flash",
          "bg": "ink",
          "line": "Weak sells more",
          "props": [
            "bill",
            "chartUp"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s8"
    },
    {
      "narration": "So knowing all that, would you actually want your money to be worth less?",
